update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head, with the City Accountant and the EOC. **Purpose:** Submit the report required by RA 12287 IRR Rule VI Sec. 1 on time, complete and consistent with the books, and learn from the declaration.\n\n**Table 7.26**\n\n*SOP 7-06 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                                          |\n|---------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-LIFT-REPORT (existing, Chapter 1 SOP GOV-05) for lifting and submission; this SOP sets compilation and follow-through |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | City Mayor signs; OCD receives (route to be confirmed with OCD VIII)                                                               |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head; M&E unit                                                                                                              |\n| **Trigger**                     | Lifting of a State of Imminent Disaster (GOV-F12)                                                                                  |\n| **Forms**                       | GOV-F13; FIN-F06 closure; ME-F03; Annex 7-D                                                                                        |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A10.8 (0, High); A4.6 (0, High)                                                                                                    |\n| **Functional MR links**         | MR-16; MR-07; MR-11                                                                                                                |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 12287; IRR Rule VI Sec. 1; Rule V Sec. 3                                                                                        |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 1 SOP GOV-05; Chapter 6 SOP 6-05 step 8; SOP 7-04                                                                          |\n\n**Table 7.27**\n\n*SOP 7-06 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Start the clock</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Record the lifting date and the 45-day due date in the reporting calendar.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Lifting recorded on GOV-F12?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> GOV-F12</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F06 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> On lifting</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Due date computed in Asia/Manila time</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Compile status</th>\n<th>EOC with M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Compile declaration status: hazard, area, dates, PDRA basis, AA measures carried out and their lead offices.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Every AA measure accounted for?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> MODE declaration and AA action records</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Status section</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 15 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Sourced to records</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Compile AA fund use</th>\n<th>City Accountant with Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Total AA spending by source and measure; unused AA funds transferred to the STF.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Totals match the books and FIN-F06?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> FIN-F06; vouchers</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Fund section</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 20 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Reconciled with the Accountant</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Accountant</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Estimate costs minimised</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit with sector offices</th>\n<th><p>Estimate economic and social costs minimised, with method and assumptions stated.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Method stated and repeatable?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> PDRA scenario; post-event data</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Costs-minimised section</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 30 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Estimates labelled as estimates</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Review and sign</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head; City Mayor</th>\n<th><p>Review the report (Annex 7-D outline); the Mayor signs.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Complete?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Draft</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Signed report; GOV-F13</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 40 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Second reader checks figures</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Submit</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Submit by the confirmed route; record the reference and date on GOV-F13.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Submitted by day 45?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Signed report</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Submission proof</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> By day 45</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Late submission reported to the CDRRMC</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Learn</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Feed findings into the AAR (SOP 7-04) and CAPA register; update the event and loss database.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Lessons recorded?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Report</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F05; ME-F07 entries</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 15 days of submission</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Linked to the report</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** ME-F06 entry; status, fund and costs-minimised sections; signed report; GOV-F13 with submission proof; CAPA and database entries.\n\n## SOP 7-07 \\| Disaster event and loss database maintenance\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Research and Planning (M&E unit). **Purpose:** Keep one standard, sourced record of every disaster that affected the City, for planning, risk assessment and Sendai monitoring.\n\n**Table 7.28**\n\n*SOP 7-07 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                               |\n|---------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-SOP7-07 (proposed); proposed MODE event and loss tables                                    |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMO Head approves the database standard; the CDRRMC receives annual summaries                        |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | M&E unit                                                                                                |\n| **Trigger**                     | Final SitRep of an event; completion of RDANA, DROMIC or PDNA; back-loading plan; each January and July |\n| **Forms**                       | ME-F07; Annex 7-E                                                                                       |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A5.4 (0, Medium)                                                                                        |\n| **Functional MR links**         | MR-03; MR-07; MR-18                                                                                     |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121 Sec. 12(c); Sendai Framework indicators; DesInventar methodology; RA 10173                     |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 3 (CDRA); Chapter 4 (SitReps); Chapter 5 (PDNA)                                                 |\n\n**Table 7.29**\n\n*SOP 7-07 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Adopt the standard</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Adopt the field list of Annex 7-E and the PSGC barangay list.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Fields cover the Sendai indicators the City reports?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Annex 7-E</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Approved standard</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Once; reviewed annually</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> CDRRMO Head approves</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> —</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Back-load</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Enter past events from the 10-Year Plan, CDRA, RDANA and PDNA reports, oldest first.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Figure plausible and sourced? If not, flag it.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Past reports</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F07 records</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> By end of 2027</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each figure carries its source</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Record new events</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Enter each new event from the final SitRep, DROMIC and RDANA; update after the PDNA.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Aggregate counts only?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Final SitRep; DROMIC; RDANA; PDNA</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F07 record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 30 days of the final SitRep</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Version history kept</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Check quality</th>\n<th>Second person in Research and Planning</th>\n<th><p>Check totals against sources and flag inconsistencies.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Consistent?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Records</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Quality log</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each January and July</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Flags resolved or noted</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Use and share</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Produce summaries for the annual report, the CDRA update and Sendai monitoring.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Summary needs small-count review? Ask the DPO.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Database</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Summaries</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each January</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> DPO review where needed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Database standard; ME-F07 records with sources; quality log; summaries.\n\n## SOP 7-08 \\| Lessons, peer learning and Manual revision\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Research and Planning, with the Manual custodian. **Purpose:** Turn lessons from the City''s own events and from other LGUs and networks into documented changes, including new versions of this Manual.\n\n**Table 7.30**\n\n*SOP 7-08 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                                 |\n|---------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-SOP7-08 (proposed); MODE Library versions                                                                    |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMO Head approves Manual versions; CDRRMC or the Mayor for changes needing an issuance                                 |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | M&E unit; Manual custodian                                                                                                |\n| **Trigger**                     | An approved AAR or IAT result; a peer exchange or network event; a change in law; the annual lessons review each February |\n| **Forms**                       | ME-F08; ME-F05                                                                                                            |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A10.9 (2, Low); A10.6 (2, Medium)                                                                                         |\n| **Functional MR links**         | MR-11; MR-18; MR-01                                                                                                       |\n| **Policy basis**                | UNDRR Scorecard 6.6.1; MCR2030; RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)                                                                       |\n| **Cross-references**            | All chapters; Chapter 8 (networks); Chapter 1 (document control)                                                          |\n\n**Table 7.31**\n\n*SOP 7-08 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Capture</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Record each lesson with its source and the change proposed.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is a change proposed? If not, it is an observation, not yet a lesson.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> AAR; IAT; exchange report</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F08 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 15 days of the source</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Source linked</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Record peer exchanges</th>\n<th>Participant</th>\n<th><p>After an exchange or network event, record what was learned and its relevance to Ormoc.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Relevant to a gap or a procedure?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Event materials</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F08 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 10 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Change proposed or "none"</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> M&amp;E unit</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Decide</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Decide whether to change a plan, form, procedure, training or MODE rule; open a CAPA entry if so.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Change within CDRRMO authority? If not, refer to the CDRRMC.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> ME-F08</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Decision; ME-F05 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Monthly</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Decision recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Revise the Manual</th>\n<th>Manual custodian</th>\n<th><p>Draft the change as a new version in the Library; update the revision record and traceability links.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Does the change alter authority or legal readings? Then the City Legal Office reviews.</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Decision</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Draft version</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 30 days of the decision</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Approved versions are never edited</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Legal Office</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Approve and communicate</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Approve the version; brief affected staff and offices.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Approved?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Draft version</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Approved version; briefing record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> On approval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Only the CDRRMO Head approves</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> —</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Review annually</th>\n<th>M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>In February, review the lessons register: lessons with no change, changes with no effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Patterns found?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> ME-F08; ME-F05</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Annual lessons review</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> February</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Presented to the CDRRMC</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** ME-F08 lessons register; decisions; CAPA entries; Manual versions and revision records; briefing records; annual lessons review.\n\n## SOP 7-09 \\| Protection of DRRM data: notices, sharing and breach response\n\n**Process owner:** City Data Protection Officer, with the CDRRMO privacy compliance officer. **Purpose:** Handle personal data in DRRM lawfully and securely, and respond to breaches as the NPC requires.\n\n**Table 7.32**\n\n*SOP 7-09 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                          |\n|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-SOP7-09 (proposed)                                                                    |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | City Mayor as personal information controller acting through the DPO; NPC for breach notifications |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | City DPO; CDRRMO privacy compliance officer                                                        |\n| **Trigger**                     | New form or data flow; new data-sharing need; annual review; a suspected breach                    |\n| **Forms**                       | ME-F09                                                                                             |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A5.5 (2, Medium)                                                                                   |\n| **Functional MR links**         | MR-15; MR-10; MR-07                                                                                |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10173 and IRR; NPC Circular No. 16-03; NPC Circular No. 2023-06                                 |\n| **Cross-references**            | Section 12; Chapters 4 and 5 (registration and relief forms); Chapter 6 (distribution records)     |\n\n**Table 7.33**\n\n*SOP 7-09 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Map the data</th>\n<th>Privacy compliance officer</th>\n<th><p>List DRRM forms and systems that hold personal data, with purpose, office and retention.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is each item necessary for its purpose?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Forms; systems</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Data inventory (ME-F09 part A)</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Annually</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> DPO reviews</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Notify</th>\n<th>Owning office with DPO</th>\n<th><p>Add privacy notices to registration, evacuation and relief forms.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Notice states purpose, sharing and retention?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Forms</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Revised forms</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before the typhoon season</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> DPO approves the text</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Secure</th>\n<th>City ICT office; platform custodian</th>\n<th><p>Apply role-based access, logging and encryption; review access lists.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Access limited to need?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Access lists</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Access review record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Quarterly</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> NPC Circular No. 2023-06 measures</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Agree sharing</th>\n<th>City Legal Office with DPO</th>\n<th><p>Sign data-sharing agreements with offices and partners that exchange personal data with the CDRRMO.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Agreement in place before sharing?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Sharing needs</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Signed agreements (ME-F09 part B)</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before sharing</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Register of agreements</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Administrator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Contain a breach</th>\n<th>Office that finds it; DPO</th>\n<th><p>Report a suspected breach to the DPO at once; contain it.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Personal data affected?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Incident</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Breach log (ME-F09 part C)</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Immediately</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Time of knowledge recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> DPO</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Assess and notify</th>\n<th>DPO</th>\n<th><p>Assess risk; where notification is required, notify the NPC and affected data subjects.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Notification required under NPC Circular No. 16-03?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Breach log</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Notifications</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 72 hours of knowledge</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Copy of notifications kept</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Learn</th>\n<th>DPO with M&amp;E unit</th>\n<th><p>Record causes and corrective actions in the CAPA register.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Action identified?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Breach log</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F05 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 15 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Closed only when effective</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Data inventory; revised forms; access reviews; data-sharing agreements; breach log; notifications; CAPA entries.\n\n# 15. Responsibility Assignment (RACI)\n\n"A" is the single proposed process-accountable owner; "R" performs; "C" is consulted; "I" is informed. The RACI allocates work; it does not transfer legal powers.\n\n**Table 7.34**\n\n*RACI for Monitoring, Evaluation and Learning*\n\n| **Activity**                           | **CC** | **MY** | **HD** | **ME** | **TWG** | **EOC** | **AS** | **VA** | **DPO** | **ACC** |\n|----------------------------------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------|---------|--------|--------|---------|---------|\n| LDRRMP indicator set and annual report | A      | I      | R      | R      | R       | I       | –      | –      | C       | C       |\n| IAT fieldwork and scoring              | I      | –      | A      | R      | C       | C       | R      | –      | C       | –       |\n| IAT validation and release             | I      | –      | A      | R      | C       | C       | C      | R      | –       | –       |\n| After-action review                    | I      | I      | A      | R      | C       | R       | –      | –      | –       | –       |\n| CAPA register                          | C      | I      | A      | R      | R       | R       | –      | –      | –       | C       |\n| 45-day post-declaration report         | I      | A      | R      | R      | C       | R       | –      | –      | –       | R       |\n| Event and loss database                | I      | –      | A      | R      | C       | C       | –      | –      | C       | –       |\n| Lessons and Manual revision            | C      | I      | A      | R      | C       | C       | –      | –      | –       | –       |\n| Data protection and breach response    | I      | A      | R      | C      | I       | C       | –      | –      | R       | –       |\n\n*Note.* CC = CDRRMC; MY = City Mayor; HD = CDRRMO Head; ME = M&E unit (CDRRMO Research and Planning); TWG = CDRRMP Technical Working Group focal offices; EOC = EOC Manager and staff; AS = assessors; VA = validators; DPO = City Data Protection Officer; ACC = City Accountant. For data protection, the Mayor is accountable as head of the personal information controller, acting through the DPO.\n\n# 16. Performance Monitoring, Quality Assurance and Corrective Action\n\nThis chapter measures itself with the same discipline it applies to others.\n\n**Table 7.35**\n\n*Performance Measures for Chapter 7*\n\n| **Measure**                                                         | **Evidence**                      | **Review owner**  |\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|-------------------|\n| Annual LDRRMP results report presented in January                   | ME-F02; CDRRMC resolution         | CDRRMC            |\n| Share of LDRRMP indicators with a baseline and current value        | ME-F01                            | CDRRMO Head       |\n| IAT cycle completed and validated on schedule; no self-validation   | MODE cycle record; validation log | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Share of triggers with an approved AAR within the set timing        | AAR register; ME-F03, ME-F04      | CDRRMO Head       |\n| CAPA items overdue; items closed as effective; recurring findings   | ME-F05                            | CDRRMC, quarterly |\n| 45-day reports submitted by day 45                                  | GOV-F13; submission proof         | CDRRMC; OCD VIII  |\n| Mandated reports submitted on time                                  | ME-F06                            | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Events in the database with sourced figures                         | ME-F07; quality log               | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Lessons with a documented change                                    | ME-F08                            | CDRRMO Head       |\n| Data-sharing agreements in place; breaches notified within 72 hours | ME-F09                            | DPO               |\n\n# 17. Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities\n\n**Table 7.36**\n\n*Implementation Priorities for Chapter 7*\n\n| **No.** | **Action**                                                                                                                                                     | **Office**                                 | **IAT**      | **When**                                         |\n|---------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|--------------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Prepare the 45-day report template (Annex 7-D, GOV-F13) and confirm the reporting route with OCD VIII.                                                         | CDRRMO Head                                | A10.8        | Before the workshop                              |\n| 2       | Hold the validation workshop under SOP 7-03; re-score the FGD-only items with evidence first.                                                                  | CDRRMO Head; M&E unit                      | All          | 1–4 December 2026                                |\n| 3       | Designate the M&E unit and the AAR facilitators by office order.                                                                                               | CDRRMO Head                                | A10.4, A10.6 | December 2026                                    |\n| 4       | Produce the first annual LDRRMP results report (ME-F02) with the ME-F01 matrix and baseline.                                                                   | M&E unit; TWG focal offices                | A10.4        | January 2027                                     |\n| 5       | Open the CAPA register (ME-F05) and load the IAT High and Medium gaps.                                                                                         | M&E unit                                   | MR-14        | December 2026                                    |\n| 6       | Attach existing AAR reports and the plan revisions they produced, for validation.                                                                              | CDRRMO                                     | A10.6, B7.4  | Before the workshop                              |\n| 7       | Confirm the DPO designation; sign data-sharing agreements with CSWDO and CPDO; add privacy notices.                                                            | City Administrator; DPO; City Legal Office | A5.5         | First quarter 2027                               |\n| 8       | Adopt the event and loss database standard and back-load events from 1991.                                                                                     | M&E unit                                   | A5.4         | Standard by March 2027; back-load by end of 2027 |\n| 9       | Record changes adopted from MCR2030, NRC and Project TRANSFORM exchanges.                                                                                      | M&E unit                                   | A10.9        | Next annual lessons review                       |\n| 10      | Platform: add root cause, verification and effectiveness fields to actions (or a CAPA table); add event and loss tables; load templates for SOPs 7-01 to 7-09. | Platform data custodian                    | MR-11, MR-14 | Before the first annual report                   |\n\nValidation: each SOP is reviewed by the offices named in its control block, the AAR procedure is tested in the first exercise after adoption, and the data-protection procedure is reviewed by the DPO and the City Legal Office before adoption.\n\n# 18. Forms, Registers and Annexes\n\n**Table 7.37**\n\n*Chapter 7 Forms and Registers*\n\n| **Code** | **Form or register**                                                | **Used in**          | **MODE**                             |\n|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| ME-F01   | LDRRMP M&E matrix (aligned with Form 5D of the 10-Year Plan)        | SOP 7-01             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F02   | Annual LDRRMP progress and results report                           | SOP 7-01             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F03   | After-action review report (full and focused forms)                 | SOP 7-04             | Proposed; receives ER-F06            |\n| ME-F04   | Exercise evaluation report (full and short forms)                   | SOP 7-04             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F05   | Corrective and preventive action (CAPA) register entry              | SOPs 7-03 to 7-09    | Proposed; MODE actions for IAT items |\n| ME-F06   | Reporting calendar and compliance tracker                           | Section 10; SOP 7-06 | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F07   | Disaster event and loss record                                      | SOP 7-07             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F08   | Lessons and peer-learning register entry                            | SOP 7-08             | Proposed                             |\n| ME-F09   | DRRM data inventory, sharing register and breach log (parts A to C) | SOP 7-09             | Proposed                             |\n| GOV-F13  | Post-lifting 45-day report (Chapter 1, Annex 1-G)                   | SOP 7-06             | Seeded                               |\n| ER-F06   | After-action and corrective action record (Chapter 4)               | SOPs 7-04, 7-05      | Seeded                               |\n\nAnnexes: **7-A** IAT and master requirements traceability; **7-B** LDRRMP M&E matrix template; **7-C** after-action review report outline; **7-D** 45-day post-declaration report outline; **7-E** disaster event and loss database fields.\n\n# 19. Relationship with Other Chapters\n\n**Table 7.38**\n\n*Links Between Chapter 7 and the Other Chapters*\n\n| **Ch.** | **Title**                                                                 | **Link**                                                                                                                                         |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability           | Defines the CAPA register, governance KPIs and records management that this chapter operates; GOV-05 and PR-LIFT-REPORT start the 45-day report. |\n| 2       | CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and HR Management               | Staffs the M&E unit; receives AAR findings on staffing and rosters.                                                                              |\n| 3       | Risk Intelligence, Planning and Institutional Preparedness                | Owns the LDRRMP and CDRA that this chapter monitors; receives the event and loss database for risk assessment.                                   |\n| 4       | Early Warning, EOC Activation, Incident Management and Emergency Response | Sends the hot wash, ER-F06 and SitReps; receives AAR findings.                                                                                   |\n| 5       | Recovery, Rehabilitation and Build Back Better                            | Sends recovery monitoring and closeout lessons; receives PDNA data back through the database.                                                    |\n| 6       | DRRM Financing, Resource Management and Accountability                    | Sends utilisation reports and COA findings; receives corrective actions on funds, stocks and inventory.                                          |\n| 8       | Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships                     | Manages the networks whose exchanges this chapter records.                                                                                       |\n| 9       | Public Awareness, Community Resilience and Capacity Development           | Runs the exercise program that this chapter evaluates; delivers training actions from the CAPA register.                                         |\n| 10      | Institutional Sustainability, Deep Resilience and Recognition             | Uses IAT results, AARs and the CAPA record as evidence for recognition systems and the improvement agenda.                                       |\n\n# 20. Concluding Notes\n\nThe City has the pieces of a learning system: a results-based M&E design in its 10-Year Plan, a Council with the duty to monitor, a working group with thematic focal offices, regular reports to OCD and the DILG, and now a full institutional baseline. What it lacks is the loop that ties them together: one register, one calendar, one database, and the habit of closing an action only when it has worked.\n\nWriting these procedures does not implement them. Until the first annual results report has been presented, the first validated IAT cycle has fed the CAPA register, one event or exercise has gone through an AAR to verified closure, and the 45-day report template has been agreed with OCD VIII, this chapter remains a controlled working draft.\n\n# References\n\nThe official text governs.\n\nArgyris, C., & Schön, D. A. (1978). *Organizational learning: A theory of action perspective*. Addison-Wesley.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2023). *Ormoc City disaster risk reduction and management ten-year plan (2023–2032)*.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026a). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC institutional assessment tool* (Version 1.7) \\[Unpublished assessment workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026b). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC master requirements traceability and 140-indicator data dictionary* (Version 1.2) \\[Unpublished project reference workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026c). *MODE architecture decision records ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-014 and ADR-029* \\[Repository documents, version 1.16.0\\]. https://github.com/asilvainnovations/ormoc-drrmo\n\nCity Government of Ormoc, Office of the City Mayor. (2022–2024). *Executive Order Nos. 2022-00020, 2023-0026 and 2024-032A*.\n\nDepartment of the Interior and Local Government Region VIII. (2025). *Adoption of the harmonized disaster response reporting template and SOP* (Memorandum R08-LGCDD-2025-02-26-008).\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2017). *Memorandum No. 147, s. 2017*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2018). *Memorandum No. 131, s. 2018: Guidelines on the establishment, operationalization and management of the emergency operations center*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2020). *National disaster risk reduction and management plan 2020–2030* and its results-based monitoring and evaluation plan.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2022). *LDRRMP formulation guidebook*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2026). *Implementing rules and regulations of Republic Act No. 12287* (signed 14 September 2026).\n\nNational Privacy Commission. (2016). *Circular No. 16-03: Personal data breach management*.\n\nNational Privacy Commission. (2023). *Circular No. 2023-06: Security of personal data in the government and the private sector*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 9470. (2007). *National Archives of the Philippines Act of 2007*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10121. (2010). *Philippine Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Act of 2010*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10173. (2012). *Data Privacy Act of 2012*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12287. (2025). *Declaration of State of Imminent Disaster Act*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2015). *Sendai framework for disaster risk reduction 2015–2030*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2017). *Disaster resilience scorecard for cities: Detailed level assessment*.\n'
